  "correspondence": [
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-1",
      "end_character": 203,
      "excerpt": "Authority lifecycle axis is not a complete status schema and does not make\nevery artifact an ontology node. It gives the minimum separations that future\nschemas, ledgers, and constitutions must preserve.",
      "unit_id": "unit-d559a211129dc1e12aaf5a5b2c19d0c073c985ffe57b4d263d7b390977c7d808"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-2",
      "end_character": 251,
      "excerpt": "Candidate Definition reconstructed from an accepted normalization scaffold and exact CyberAlchemy-v2 source sections. It is not admitted and grants no implementation, migration, registry, publication, release, deployment, or external-effect authority.",
      "unit_id": "unit-551051d584e8331e5ddcc495261d314ed89f7cf4cc2e9b5d89d0ceba64f24fbe"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-3",
      "end_character": 304,
      "excerpt": "Use authority lifecycle axes when evaluating definitions, constitutions, axioms,\nontology nodes, inventory cards, task results, schemas, and implementation\nclaims. The reviewer should ask which axis is being advanced: source role,\nmaturity, evidence, owner commitment, provenance, or canonical authority.",
      "unit_id": "unit-8642c98be289f01ca5cec6b463c2d4635a87f10aeb26e2d7754d0784c99e546e"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-4",
      "end_character": 22,
      "excerpt": "scope.shared-authority",
      "unit_id": "unit-d98b0dcc8c90b5d742e9beb805c5005c88770dc54b7c3939d5b7cc2388378d48"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-5",
      "end_character": 78,
      "excerpt": "Admission, activation, publication, release, deployment, and external effects.",
      "unit_id": "unit-8dec732fb5d927545d4bf5c1bea73405d34e388983cdba3240a36b63ba348803"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-6",
      "end_character": 88,
      "excerpt": "Meanings assigned to split or reclassified sibling targets unless explicitly referenced.",
      "unit_id": "unit-94bf2030418c421474ce1629a5f3255fde290758d03623f29467345f93ee9ea0"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-7",
      "end_character": 111,
      "excerpt": "Resolve semantic.governance-axis-independence-invariant by its machine identity rather than its directory name.",
      "unit_id": "unit-074a5e6d0208003ba9d2599658501fbdf9d23247483e8586965326ea65c6d10e"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-8",
      "end_character": 107,
      "excerpt": "Challenge source drift through the L1 drift audit before relying on Governance-Axis Independence Invariant.",
      "unit_id": "unit-2693910ee108c64c532b70268f294b2f65b2743287b2146d88153709db5cc03e"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-9",
      "end_character": 716,
      "excerpt": "In CyberAlchemy-lab migration work, Governance-Axis Independence Invariant is a prototype meaning reconstructed from CAL-NORMALIZE-01. It remains non-authoritative until the correct Lab owner admits a fully validated candidate.\n\nSource context retained for reconstruction:\n\nIn CyberAlchemy v2, this definition absorbs the imported vault's mature split\nbetween `node_type`, `status`, evidence confidence, and commitment language as a\nlocal lifecycle principle. The source vocabulary is evidence, while CAV2 keeps\nthe more general axis split so Arcanum, DomainSpec, house_project, ontology,\ninventory, Craft, and future implementation artifacts can share one governance\nshape without sharing one exact status taxonomy.",
      "unit_id": "unit-2a155408b28acd65a9ad9900306f7671de56fa928e1f25a5cac8b3fdc79efaac"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-10",
      "end_character": 41,
      "excerpt": "/home/vrondelli/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab",
      "unit_id": "unit-ffa309e64b53ab85866dd9c0bce78b5cb2d9a40913e906c9ea92bc3faa5b2ed5"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-11",
      "end_character": 125,
      "excerpt": "\"Useful\", \"trusted\", \"finished\", \"owned\", and \"canonical\" are different words.\nDo not let one of them impersonate the others.",
      "unit_id": "unit-56856c4187c32b7b52d6d010a578be26b9ed0d46e104f647a8a97565063fe8fe"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-12",
      "end_character": 203,
      "excerpt": "Authority lifecycle axis is not a complete status schema and does not make\nevery artifact an ontology node. It gives the minimum separations that future\nschemas, ledgers, and constitutions must preserve.",
      "unit_id": "unit-ec6a20802289b935174ab5961cc5b6c668ff86cade3cee1a1ebc504f26735e78"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-13",
      "end_character": 369,
      "excerpt": "An authority-bearing artifact `a` has lifecycle posture:\n\n```text\nL(a) = (kind, status, evidence, commitment, provenance, owner, residue)\n```\n\nwhere each component may be known, unknown, deferred, or source-local. A\ngovernance move is valid only if it changes the intended component and does not\nimply changes to the others unless those changes are explicitly recorded.",
      "unit_id": "unit-2f4055fb6d2b8213f878b4174c0625af6aee3bfcf304514ef48c618780342701"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-14",
      "end_character": 942,
      "excerpt": "Governance-Axis Independence Invariant is the normalized invariant identified by semantic.governance-axis-independence-invariant, owned within scope.shared-authority, and carried by type.invariant. Any canonical instance must preserve that classification and the accepted source relations to CAV2-D23 without silently merging it with another target.\n\nBound source-semantic basis:\n\nAuthority lifecycle axis is the CyberAlchemy v2 rule that authority posture must\nseparate at least these dimensions when they matter to a decision:\n\n- role or kind\n- maturity or status\n- evidence confidence\n- commitment or conviction\n- provenance\n- owner\n\nNo one axis may silently stand in for another. A definition can be mature but\nweakly evidenced, an imported source can be well-evidenced but not locally\ncanonical, an ontology candidate can be useful but unpromoted, and an owner can\nbe committed to a hypothesis without that hypothesis becoming authority.",
      "unit_id": "unit-1a12e1793a0fea27817b47e1110062d0685a69e1ca4d5290ed9f5d0c7308ba3e"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-15",
      "end_character": 70,
      "excerpt": "Stable normalized identity for Governance-Axis Independence Invariant.",
      "unit_id": "unit-b06322abe5e178086ea5763fd3244cd07d7388d8d9f57863c7ae223462c00735"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-16",
      "end_character": 47,
      "excerpt": "semantic.governance-axis-independence-invariant",
      "unit_id": "unit-2d29bf515c3bff23d3a8b201a1b4b7ca3d4d1f1bb49a2f5f899f1f78726a5ca3"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-17",
      "end_character": 49,
      "excerpt": "Bound CyberAlchemy-v2 source-definition identity.",
      "unit_id": "unit-589257840cd95cd1a238672e86bd6b9137eba67d8ce5929322ef98c2127693fd"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-18",
      "end_character": 8,
      "excerpt": "CAV2-D23",
      "unit_id": "unit-95527dd3f52754ce73e26b04348ce5f493d366dde22ab790d4612610c9e46ec3"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-19",
      "end_character": 85,
      "excerpt": "The candidate identity remains cal.definition.governance-axis-independence-invariant.",
      "unit_id": "unit-57ea68fea272c8d55a8f006bb9eb30b7f3c061571912ab024c6c2477903bba9d"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-20",
      "end_character": 53,
      "excerpt": "Every selected source-section digest remains current.",
      "unit_id": "unit-62d9b9f0f2e14b44077e3a0db7904079fca058376b549a92223861c2220f97bc"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-21",
      "end_character": 51,
      "excerpt": "The machine record validates against Definition/v1.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6e0a36a3e7ce10e3274f2fe9e2ee41f7701f2c203d126d1278b94a5f3bd6b8fd"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-22",
      "end_character": 68,
